⚠️ Behavior:
When the button bounces, the capacitor filters the voltage transition.

GPIO sees a gradual transition, not multiple toggles.

2. schmitt trigger
🧠 Why Use a Schmitt Trigger?
When a push button is pressed or released, contact bounce causes noisy voltage transitions. Even RC filters might not clean this entirely under noisy conditions.

A Schmitt Trigger solves this using hysteresis — it only toggles output when the input crosses clearly defined thresholds. This eliminates rapid toggling.

